in the new movie the batman bruce wayne  quickly meets and partners up with  selena kyle also known to dc fans as  catwoman the two have an intensely  intertwined story with bruce helping  selena uncover the fate of her roommate  and the truth about her father carmine  falcone  but there's one other important figure  in selena's life who plays a key role in  the film's story and she never even  shows up on screen this is her mother  maria kyle selena explains her backstory  to bruce one night telling him about how  her mother worked at the iceberg lounge  and met falcone there of course then  this romance led to her and she spends  most of her early childhood years just  hanging out at the establishment as she  talks about her history it becomes clear  that a lot of what she does is based  around his past experience while she  might claim to want to get away from  gotham selena can't seem to leave her  connection to falcone and what happened  to her mother behind it's obvious that  selena loves her mother very dearly  leading her to take her father's  abandonment more personally then when  her roommate ends up dead in a similar  fashion as her mother selena's drive for  answers grows even stronger but casual  fans of the dc eu tuning in to watch the  batman might not know a lot about  selena's backstory and there's a lot  about her mother maria that the movie  doesn't go into in the batman viewers  only really know anything about maria  based on what selena describes to bruce  or falcone but with all the information  the movie provides it appears that this  version of maria is a loving mother who  is just unlucky in life maria works at  the iceberg lounge both before and after  giving birth to selena but unfortunately  she is murdered when selena is very  young and for a long time selena doesn't  know who is responsible without a real  direction in life selena grows up and  develops the thieving skills she  exhibits in the movie intending to steal  some cash leave gotham and start over  aside from her career and relationship  with falcone the batman doesn't reveal  too much else about selena's mother  but one thing is crystal clear and  that's the fact that selena clearly  loves her mother very much and holds no  resentment or bad feelings over how she  grows up instead all of her grief hate  and loneliness is targeted at falcone  who she knows is her father but who had  zero involvement in her life leaving her  to grow up all alone after maria's death  in the comics selena's relationship with  her mother is a little more complicated  and if you can't believe it a little  more traumatic too as revealed in the  solo series catwoman volume 2 which ran  from 1993 to 2001 when selena was a  child her mother maria was in an abusive  marriage with selena's father brian kyle  at one point brian says that maria's  family are refugees possibly from cuba  and she likely speaks both english and  spanish something brian berrata for  along with that maria suffers from  mental illness and faces money pressures  to support the family which includes a  younger sister selena doesn't have in  the film named maggie kyle unfortunately  maria dies by suicide when selena is  very young and she is the one to  discover her in the aftermath of her  mother's death selena's father turns to  drinking and she is eventually separated  from her sister leading to her growing  up on the street and taking up thievery  luckily selena holds on to one  connection to her mother in the form of  gymnastics which her mother enrolls her  in before her death selena exhibits a  natural skill for gymnastics and it  clearly helps her later on when she  becomes catwoman in the comics there's  also a rumor that carmine falcone and  his wife louisa falcone are selena's  real parents though it's never confirmed  and of course a film makes it clear that  falcone is at least her father relating  to that the comics don't show if or how  maria and falcone could have crossed  paths although their connection is a  major focus of selena's story in the  batman if you or anyone you know is  having suicidal thoughts please call or  chat online with the national suicide  prevention lifeline at 1-800-273-talk  8255 or text home to the crisis text  line 741 741
 

